Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: So that would be Subic, Clark,

asr-002325
01:59:48.180 --> 01:59:50.180
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Batangas, Laguna.

asr-002326
01:59:50.180 --> 01:59:52.180
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: The industrial heart

asr-002327
01:59:52.180 --> 01:59:54.180
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: of the Philippine economy ay

asr-002328
01:59:54.180 --> 01:59:56.180
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: ibibigay daw sa Paxilica.

asr-002329
01:59:56.180 --> 01:59:58.180
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: No? So,

asr-002330
02:00:00.000 --> 02:00:09.720
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Ang tanong dito ngayon, and this is a question that pertains to the primary mandate of the Department of National Defense and the AFP,

asr-002331
02:00:10.940 --> 02:00:18.520
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: paano didepensahan ang mga ito kung magkaroon ng gera sa pagitan ng US at Pilipinas?

asr-002332
02:00:19.400 --> 02:00:23.440
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Napakita sa Gulf na wasak yan.

asr-002333
02:00:24.500 --> 02:00:27.460
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Let me, another, one last.

asr-002334
02:00:27.460 --> 02:00:31.920
Deputy Speaker Yevgeny Vincente B. Emano: Sorry, before you continue, I would like to request the gentleman to wrap up, please.

asr-002335
02:00:31.920 --> 02:00:33.720
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Opo, we're wrapping up.

asr-002336
02:00:34.500 --> 02:00:37.680
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: A few other points.

asr-002337
02:00:39.240 --> 02:00:41.200
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: So, napakita natin.

asr-002338
02:00:42.820 --> 02:00:44.360
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: One last slide.

asr-002339
02:00:46.080 --> 02:00:49.740
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Even, so mukhang, dalawa actually.

asr-002340
02:00:50.920 --> 02:00:52.140
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: One is tidal wave.

asr-002341
02:00:53.160 --> 02:00:54.140
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Tidal wave.

asr-002342
02:00:55.200 --> 02:00:55.480
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Okay.

asr-002343
02:00:55.480 --> 02:00:55.600
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Okay.

asr-002344
02:00:55.600 --> 02:00:57.880
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: What is tidal wave?

asr-002345
02:00:57.980 --> 02:01:06.780
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Tidal wave was a recent major report issued by Heritage, the Washington think tank, the renowned Washington think tank.

asr-002346
02:01:07.660 --> 02:01:10.480
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Tungkol ito, 400 pages ito.

asr-002347
02:01:10.580 --> 02:01:17.600
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: This is a study on logistics, China, logistics of China and the US in time of war.

asr-002348
02:01:18.480 --> 02:01:24.320
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Kung magkaroon daw ng gera, ano mangyayari sa, ano maging risulta from the point of view of logistics?

asr-002349
02:01:24.320 --> 02:01:25.360
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Ano ang sabi?

asr-002350
02:01:25.600 --> 02:01:26.180
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Dito.

asr-002351
02:01:27.020 --> 02:01:39.580
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Ang sabi dito ay, sabi ng Heritage Foundation, hindi daw tatagal ng isang linggo ang ammunition supplies ng US in an all-out war with China.

asr-002352
02:01:40.180 --> 02:01:40.820
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: One week.

asr-002353
02:01:41.660 --> 02:01:50.960
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: And then, hindi tatagal daw ng isang buwan ang kanilang fuel supply in a war with China.

asr-002354
02:01:51.280 --> 02:01:55.160
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: This was issued by Heritage, as you can see, in January.

asr-002355
02:01:55.600 --> 02:01:57.040
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: 2026.

asr-002356
02:02:01.020 --> 02:02:02.600
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Before the Iran War.

asr-002357
02:02:03.440 --> 02:02:06.120
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: So ngayon, mas kinumpirman ng realidad.

asr-002358
02:02:06.860 --> 02:02:16.080
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Kung Iran pa lang ang kalaban, medyo naubusan na ng bala at hirap na ng logistics ang US.

asr-002359
02:02:16.800 --> 02:02:19.100
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Paano pa ngayon sa China?

asr-002360
02:02:19.100 --> 02:02:25.100
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: And then the final study that I would like to present here is one issued by...

asr-002361
02:02:25.600 --> 02:02:28.720
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: by the Washington think tank, again, Defense Priorities.

asr-002362
02:02:29.660 --> 02:02:37.200
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Itong think tank na ito is funded by the American billionaire Koch, the Koch brothers.

asr-002363
02:02:38.100 --> 02:02:40.020
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: These are right-wing billionaires.

asr-002364
02:02:40.280 --> 02:02:41.520
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Mas right-wing pa kay Trump.

asr-002365
02:02:42.600 --> 02:02:43.980
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Ano ang nilabas nila recently?

asr-002366
02:02:44.200 --> 02:02:50.940
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Just this September 10, they are proposing a second island chain strategy for Asia.

asr-002367
02:02:51.720 --> 02:02:51.860
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: No?

asr-002368
02:02:51.860 --> 02:02:55.300
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: What do they mean by a second island chain strategy?

asr-002369
02:02:55.600 --> 02:02:56.020
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: For Asia?

asr-002370
02:02:56.620 --> 02:03:05.600
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Sabi po dito, this is a strategy that shifts US military commitments and presence

asr-002371
02:03:05.600 --> 02:03:12.280
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: from the vulnerable first island chain toward a more defensible second island chain,

asr-002372
02:03:12.520 --> 02:03:18.100
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: which would reduce US military requirements and the risk of a war with China

asr-002373
02:03:18.100 --> 02:03:20.680
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: while still protecting US interests.

asr-002374
02:03:21.480 --> 02:03:25.100
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: And then second, the United States should narrow its defense commitments

asr-002375
02:03:25.600 --> 02:03:31.220
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: in the region, shifting to a clear non-intervention position on Taiwan,

asr-002376
02:03:32.020 --> 02:03:37.960
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: ending mutual defense alliances with South Korea, Australia, the Philippines, and Japan,

asr-002377
02:03:38.840 --> 02:03:43.520
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: and negotiating narrow and flexible security partnerships in their place.

asr-002378
02:03:44.380 --> 02:03:47.660
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: US military posture should change accordingly.

asr-002379
02:03:48.480 --> 02:03:49.560
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: So, yan na po ang posisyon.

asr-002380
02:03:49.560 --> 02:03:55.260
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Kung baga, may pagtanggap na in certain circles in Washington,

asr-002381
02:03:55.600 --> 02:03:57.360
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: the most conservative circles,

asr-002382
02:03:57.520 --> 02:04:00.800
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: sabi nila, di na kayang depensahan ng US

asr-002383
02:04:00.800 --> 02:04:04.960
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: ang first island chain, atras tayo sa second island chain.

asr-002384
02:04:05.620 --> 02:04:07.740
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Ibig sabihin nun, as far back as Guam.

asr-002385
02:04:08.600 --> 02:04:08.680
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: No?

asr-002386
02:04:10.140 --> 02:04:17.340
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: At sabi nga, huwag na, let us leave behind the mutual defense treaties

asr-002387
02:04:17.340 --> 02:04:21.540
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: because hindi na raw kayang ng US ang commitment na to.

asr-002388
02:04:21.540 --> 02:04:25.340
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: So, in favor of more to them,

asr-002389
02:04:25.600 --> 02:04:26.220
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: flexible arrangements.

asr-002390
02:04:26.420 --> 02:04:30.600
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Ito, hindi mga kaliwa ang nagpo-propose nito,

asr-002391
02:04:30.740 --> 02:04:32.960
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: yung mga pinakakanan sa US.

asr-002392
02:04:33.620 --> 02:04:36.720
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Now, my final point and question is,

asr-002393
02:04:36.800 --> 02:04:40.480
Deputy Speaker Yevgeny Vincente B. Emano: May may request sa gentleman to wrap up in the last 30 seconds, please.

asr-002394
02:04:40.500 --> 02:04:42.360
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Okay, sa ganitong realidad ngayon,

asr-002395
02:04:43.040 --> 02:04:48.200
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: tama po ba na patuloy na panindigan pa rin

asr-002396
02:04:48.200 --> 02:04:50.280
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: ng Marcos Jr. Administration

asr-002397
02:04:50.280 --> 02:04:54.080
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: at ng Department of National Defense

asr-002398
02:04:54.080 --> 02:04:55.300
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: ang kanilang,

asr-002399
02:04:55.600 --> 02:04:59.460
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: patuloy na pagkapit

asr-002400
02:04:59.460 --> 02:05:03.700
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: sa Mutual Defense Treaty with the US,

asr-002401
02:05:04.220 --> 02:05:07.180
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: given that events have shown

asr-002402
02:05:07.180 --> 02:05:11.440
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: that such a close alliance with the US

asr-002403
02:05:11.440 --> 02:05:15.480
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: would mean putting our economic infrastructure at risk

asr-002404
02:05:15.480 --> 02:05:16.460
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: and also,

asr-002405
02:05:17.280 --> 02:05:19.620
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: would also mean that

asr-002406
02:05:19.620 --> 02:05:24.000
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: the US may not be willing or able

asr-002407
02:05:24.000 --> 02:05:25.080
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: to,

asr-002408
02:05:25.600 --> 02:05:26.600
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: ah,

asr-002409
02:05:26.600 --> 02:05:28.700
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: live up to its defense commitments.

asr-002410
02:05:28.700 --> 02:05:30.300
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Hindi niya kayang ipagtanggol.

asr-002411
02:05:30.300 --> 02:05:32.300
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Katulad ng nangyari sa Middle East,

asr-002412
02:05:32.300 --> 02:05:33.720
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: hindi pinagtagol.

asr-002413
02:05:33.720 --> 02:05:34.940
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: And therefore,

asr-002414
02:05:34.940 --> 02:05:39.660
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: sa halip na patuloy na magpahipit ng relasyon sa US,

asr-002415
02:05:39.660 --> 02:05:43.240
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: ay tumindig tayo, no?

asr-002416
02:05:43.240 --> 02:05:44.680
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Labanan natin ng China,

asr-002417
02:05:44.680 --> 02:05:47.720
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: pero pangunahing umaasa sa sarili nating lakas

asr-002418
02:05:47.720 --> 02:05:49.140
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: at makipagtulungan,

asr-002419
02:05:49.140 --> 02:05:50.540
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: hindi sa US,

asr-002420
02:05:50.540 --> 02:05:53.920
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: kung hindi sa mga kapitbahay natin, halimbawa,

asr-002421
02:05:53.920 --> 02:05:54.940
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: ASEAN,

asr-002422
02:05:54.940 --> 02:05:55.940
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Malaysia,

asr-002423
02:05:55.940 --> 02:05:56.940
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Indonesia,

asr-002424
02:05:56.940 --> 02:05:57.940
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Vietnam,

asr-002425
02:05:57.940 --> 02:05:59.600
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: at iba pa.

asr-002426
02:05:59.600 --> 02:06:01.080
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: May I get a,

asr-002427
02:06:01.080 --> 02:06:04.080
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: at least a final response from the sponsor?

asr-002428
02:06:04.080 --> 02:06:06.700
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Kine-question na po natin, basically,

asr-002429
02:06:06.700 --> 02:06:08.100
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: yung, ah,

asr-002430
02:06:08.100 --> 02:06:12.580
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: pagkapit ng Marcos Jr. administration

asr-002431
02:06:12.580 --> 02:06:16.780
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: sa Mutual Defense Treaty at sa mga kano?

asr-002432
02:06:16.780 --> 02:06:17.640
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Opo.

asr-002433
02:06:17.640 --> 02:06:19.040
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: Yes, ah, Mr. Speaker,

asr-002434
02:06:19.040 --> 02:06:21.740
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: the Department takes note of the concerns

asr-002435
02:06:21.740 --> 02:06:24.780
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: and the issues raised by our distinguished colleague,

asr-002437
02:06:25.240 --> 02:06:28.740
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: ah, this is precisely the reason why we have to support

asr-002438
02:06:28.740 --> 02:06:31.160
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: ah, the AFP modernization program

asr-002439
02:06:31.160 --> 02:06:34.840
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: and the Comprehensive Archipelagic Defense Concept.

asr-002440
02:06:34.840 --> 02:06:36.400
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: This is what we want to do.

asr-002441
02:06:36.400 --> 02:06:40.560
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: We want to make sure that we protect our territory.

asr-002442
02:06:40.560 --> 02:06:41.560
Deputy Speaker Yevgeny Vincente B. Emano: Thank you.

asr-002443
02:06:41.560 --> 02:06:42.560
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Maraming salamat, Mr. Speaker.

asr-002444
02:06:42.560 --> 02:06:43.560
Deputy Speaker Yevgeny Vincente B. Emano: Thank you.

asr-002445
02:06:43.560 --> 02:06:44.740
Deputy Speaker Yevgeny Vincente B. Emano: Thank you, sir.

asr-002446
02:06:44.740 --> 02:06:45.740
Deputy Speaker Yevgeny Vincente B. Emano: Majority Leader.

asr-002447
02:06:45.740 --> 02:06:49.040
Rep. Arnan C. Panaligan: Mr. Speaker, I move that you recognize the honorable

asr-002448
02:06:49.040 --> 02:06:52.900
Rep. Arnan C. Panaligan: Sergio C. Dagooc of Party-list APEC for his interpellation.

asr-002449
02:06:52.920 --> 02:06:54.920
Deputy Speaker Yevgeny Vincente B. Emano: The gentleman from Partylist APEC,

asr-002451
02:06:54.920 --> 02:06:56.900
Deputy Speaker Yevgeny Vincente B. Emano: Representative Sergio Dagooc,

asr-002452
02:06:56.900 --> 02:06:58.900
Deputy Speaker Yevgeny Vincente B. Emano: is recognized.

asr-002453
02:06:58.900 --> 02:07:01.600
Rep. Sergio C. Dagooc: Thank you, Mr. Speaker.

asr-002454
02:07:01.600 --> 02:07:02.800
Rep. Sergio C. Dagooc: Thank you, Majority Leader.

asr-002455
02:07:02.800 --> 02:07:05.800
Rep. Sergio C. Dagooc: Magandang umaga po sa ating lahat.

asr-002456
02:07:05.800 --> 02:07:07.000
Rep. Sergio C. Dagooc: Maiksi lang po.

asr-002457
02:07:07.000 --> 02:07:08.040
Rep. Sergio C. Dagooc: Ah,

asr-002458
02:07:08.040 --> 02:07:10.300
Rep. Sergio C. Dagooc: naubos na yung mga tanong ko eh.

asr-002459
02:07:10.300 --> 02:07:11.400
Rep. Sergio C. Dagooc: Tinanong na ni,

asr-002460
02:07:11.400 --> 02:07:14.240
Rep. Sergio C. Dagooc: ng kasabahan ko eh.

asr-002461
02:07:14.240 --> 02:07:14.900
Rep. Sergio C. Dagooc: Ah,

asr-002462
02:07:14.900 --> 02:07:17.500
Rep. Sergio C. Dagooc: Distinguished Sponsor,

asr-002463
02:07:17.500 --> 02:07:19.300
Rep. Sergio C. Dagooc: Mr. Speaker,

asr-002464
02:07:19.300 --> 02:07:21.840
Rep. Sergio C. Dagooc: ang number one issue,

asr-002465
02:07:21.840 --> 02:07:24.440
Rep. Sergio C. Dagooc: ah, correct me if I'm wrong, no,

asr-002466
02:07:24.440 --> 02:07:27.280
Rep. Sergio C. Dagooc: ito yung nabasa ko.

asr-002467
02:07:27.280 --> 02:07:33.640
Rep. Sergio C. Dagooc: May performance report tayo sa Land Forces Defense Program, no.

asr-002468
02:07:33.640 --> 02:07:38.400
Rep. Sergio C. Dagooc: The performance report shows that the Philippine Army

asr-002469
02:07:38.400 --> 02:07:43.840
Rep. Sergio C. Dagooc: achieved only 64 percent of its 81 percent target

asr-002470
02:07:43.840 --> 02:07:48.800
Rep. Sergio C. Dagooc: for tactical units in prescribed readiness condition,

asr-002471
02:07:48.800 --> 02:07:54.080
Rep. Sergio C. Dagooc: and only 28 percent of its 79 percent target

asr-002472
02:07:54.080 --> 02:07:59.580
Rep. Sergio C. Dagooc: for ready reserve units in prescribed readiness condition.

asr-002473
02:07:59.580 --> 02:08:02.840
Rep. Sergio C. Dagooc: The SEAD report states that

asr-002474
02:08:02.840 --> 02:08:10.680
Rep. Sergio C. Dagooc: the shortfall was partly due to the rebump of the Philippine Army readiness rating system

asr-002475
02:08:10.680 --> 02:08:17.380
Rep. Sergio C. Dagooc: aimed at determining and resolving the capability shortfalls of existing tactical units.

asr-002476
02:08:17.380 --> 02:08:20.620
Rep. Sergio C. Dagooc: So, the question, Distinguished Sponsor,

asr-002477
02:08:20.620 --> 02:08:21.940
Rep. Sergio C. Dagooc: ah, is this.

asr-002478
02:08:21.940 --> 02:08:23.920
Rep. Sergio C. Dagooc: If the readiness rating system is not suitable,

asr-002480
02:08:23.980 --> 02:08:26.740
Rep. Sergio C. Dagooc: if the readiness rating system was changed in a way

asr-002481
02:08:26.740 --> 02:08:30.420
Rep. Sergio C. Dagooc: that lowered the reported accomplishment,

asr-002482
02:08:30.420 --> 02:08:35.440
Rep. Sergio C. Dagooc: how can we be sure that the Army's actual fighting capability

asr-002483
02:08:35.440 --> 02:08:41.120
Rep. Sergio C. Dagooc: has not been overstated in the previous years?

asr-002484
02:08:41.120 --> 02:08:52.440
Rep. Sergio C. Dagooc: Importante to sakin, dami kong mga kamag-anak dyan eh.

asr-002485
02:08:52.440 --> 02:08:53.820
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: Mr. Speaker, ah,

asr-002486
02:08:53.820 --> 02:08:55.520
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: the reason that, ah,

asr-002487
02:08:55.520 --> 02:08:58.660
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: there has to be adjustments with standards,

asr-002488
02:08:58.660 --> 02:09:03.320
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: ah, particularly because, ah, threats are also evolving.

asr-002489
02:09:03.320 --> 02:09:05.420
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: So that is the reason why, ah,

asr-002490
02:09:05.420 --> 02:09:06.880
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: besides that, ah,

asr-002491
02:09:06.880 --> 02:09:12.420
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: the scope of the mission areas also, ah, change.

asr-002492
02:09:12.420 --> 02:09:16.120
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: So that is the reason for the higher, ah,

asr-002493
02:09:16.120 --> 02:09:19.220
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: well, higher standards, really like the different standards.

asr-002494
02:09:19.220 --> 02:09:22.420
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: Ah, but there is an assurance that, ah,

asr-002495
02:09:22.420 --> 02:09:23.660
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: hindi naman po na-overstate.

asr-002496
02:09:23.660 --> 02:09:29.860
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: Yung mga, ah, mga performance, ah, indicators from previous years.

asr-002497
02:09:29.860 --> 02:09:33.920
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: It's more of ngayon lang po talaga kailangan i-adjust yung standards,

asr-002498
02:09:33.920 --> 02:09:36.960
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: ah, given nag-iiba po talaga yung mga threats

asr-002499
02:09:36.960 --> 02:09:41.120
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: and nag-iiba rin po yung scope of, ah, mission areas.

asr-002500
02:09:41.120 --> 02:09:42.660
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: Mr. Speaker.

asr-002501
02:09:42.660 --> 02:09:45.320
Rep. Sergio C. Dagooc: Ah, naintindihan ko po, no?

asr-002502
02:09:45.320 --> 02:09:53.500
Rep. Sergio C. Dagooc: Ah, however, is there, ah, concrete steps that the Department has taken

asr-002503
02:09:53.500 --> 02:09:59.860
Rep. Sergio C. Dagooc: to ensure that this revamp will actually improve unit readiness

asr-002504
02:09:59.860 --> 02:10:05.500
Rep. Sergio C. Dagooc: and not simply change the way readiness is measured on paper?

asr-002505
02:10:13.500 --> 02:10:15.500
Rep. Sergio C. Dagooc: Talagang totohanan po ito.

asr-002518
02:10:50.310 --> 02:10:52.670
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: Ah, Mr. Speaker,

asr-002519
02:10:52.670 --> 02:10:54.140
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: This is a continuing process.

